#: src/ai/inline-assistant.md:3
msgid "Inline Assistant"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/inline-assistant.md:5
msgid "Usage Overview"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/inline-assistant.md:7
msgid ""
"Use <kbd class=\"keybinding\">ctrl-enter|ctrl-enter</kbd> to open the Inline "
"Assistant in editors, text threads, the rules library, channel notes, and "
"the terminal panel."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/inline-assistant.md:9
msgid ""
"The Inline Assistant sends your current selection (or line) to a language "
"model and replaces it with the response."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/inline-assistant.md:11
msgid "Getting Started"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/inline-assistant.md:13
msgid ""
"If you're using the Inline Assistant for the first time, you need to have at "
"least one LLM provider or external agent configured. You can do that by:"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/inline-assistant.md:16
msgid ""
"[subscribing to our Pro plan](https://zed.dev/pricing), so you have access "
"to our hosted models"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/inline-assistant.md:17
msgid ""
"[using your own API keys](./llm-providers.md#use-your-own-keys), either from "
"model providers like Anthropic or model gateways like OpenRouter."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/inline-assistant.md:19
msgid ""
"If you have already set up an LLM provider to interact with [the Agent Panel]"
"(./agent-panel.md#getting-started), then that will also work for the Inline "
"Assistant."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/inline-assistant.md:21
msgid ""
"Unlike the Agent Panel, though, the only exception at the moment is "
"[external agents](./external-agents.md). They currently can't be used for "
"generating changes with the Inline Assistant."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/inline-assistant.md:24
msgid "Adding Context"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/inline-assistant.md:26
msgid ""
"You can add context in the Inline Assistant the same way you can in [the "
"Agent Panel](./agent-panel.md#adding-context):"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/inline-assistant.md:28
msgid "@-mention files, directories, past threads, rules, and symbols"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/inline-assistant.md:29
msgid "paste images that are copied on your clipboard"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/inline-assistant.md:31
msgid ""
"You can also create a thread in the Agent Panel, then reference it with "
"`@thread` in the Inline Assistant. This lets you refine a specific change "
"from a larger thread without re-explaining context."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/inline-assistant.md:33
msgid "Parallel Generations"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/inline-assistant.md:35
msgid "The Inline Assistant can generate multiple changes at once:"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/inline-assistant.md:37
msgid "Multiple Cursors"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/inline-assistant.md:39
msgid ""
"With multiple cursors, pressing <kbd class=\"keybinding\">ctrl-enter|ctrl-"
"enter</kbd> sends the same prompt to each cursor position, generating "
"changes at all locations simultaneously."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/inline-assistant.md:41
msgid "This works well with excerpts in [multibuffers](../multibuffers.md)."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/inline-assistant.md:43
msgid "Multiple Models"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/inline-assistant.md:45
msgid ""
"You can use the Inline Assistant to send the same prompt to multiple models "
"at once."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/inline-assistant.md:47
msgid ""
"Here's how you can customize your settings file ([how to edit](../"
"configuring-zed.md#settings-files)) to add this functionality:"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/inline-assistant.md:51 src/ai/inline-assistant.md:75
