#: src/ai/inline-assistant.md:66
msgid ""
"When multiple models are configured, you'll see in the Inline Assistant UI "
"buttons that allow you to cycle between outputs generated by each model."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/inline-assistant.md:68
msgid ""
"The models you specify here are always used in _addition_ to your [default "
"model](#default-model)."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/inline-assistant.md:70
msgid ""
"For example, the following configuration will generate three outputs for "
"every assist. One with Claude Sonnet 4.5 (the default model), another with "
"GPT-5-mini, and another one with Gemini 3 Flash."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/inline-assistant.md:87
msgid "\"gemini-3-flash\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/inline-assistant.md:94
msgid "Inline Assistant vs. Edit Prediction"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/inline-assistant.md:96
msgid "Both features generate inline code, but they work differently:"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/inline-assistant.md:98
msgid ""
"**Inline Assistant**: You write a prompt and select what to transform. You "
"control the context."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/inline-assistant.md:99
msgid ""
"**[Edit Prediction](./edit-prediction.md)**: Zed automatically suggests "
"edits based on your recent changes, visited files, and cursor position. No "
"prompting required."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/inline-assistant.md:101
msgid ""
"The key difference: Inline Assistant is explicit and prompt-driven; Edit "
"Prediction is automatic and context-inferred."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/inline-assistant.md:103
msgid "Prefilling Prompts"
msgstr ""

